    "canonical": "Beyond the river, attackers blocked the road. One grabbed his arm. Another swung a stick. Melos struck out, broke free, and stumbled past them. Their angry shouts followed him, but he did not look back. By afternoon, pain filled every step. Then his legs gave way. He lay with his face against the earth. The city was still far away. He could not reach it. He could not even stand. He could stay here. No one would find him before sunset. His friend would die, but he would live. For one terrible moment, the thought brought relief. Then he remembered those warm fingers around his hand.",
